🧩 Problem Statement:
"E-commerce Order Placement with Distributed Services"

A company runs an e-commerce platform with three microservices:

Order Service – accepts customer orders.

Inventory Service – checks and reserves product stock.

Payment Service – processes payments.

When a customer places an order, the following steps must occur:

The Order Service receives the order request.

It then asks the Inventory Service to reserve the requested items.

If successful, it calls the Payment Service to deduct the amount.

Once payment is successful, the order is marked as “CONFIRMED”.

However, failures can happen at any point:

If inventory is not available, the order must be cancelled.

If payment fails, the inventory reservation must be rolled back.

You need to implement this using a Saga pattern to manage data consistency across these services.

